# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a checkout on a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows
# default) materialises every text file with CRLF, while Prettier - which has no
# config here, so `endOfLine: "lf"` - insists on LF. The result is a repository
# whose own `format:check` cannot pass on Windows and passes on Linux: a gate
# that reports the platform rather than the code. `eol=lf` removes the
# conversion instead of teaching the formatter to tolerate both.
*           text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.db        binary
*.tgz       binary
